WEBVTT

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.560
JOY: And that's it. We love our girl.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.560
She's got great friends
and a great house.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.320
Things couldn't be better.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.840
After all, Riley's 11 now.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.640
What could happen?

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.400
-What...
-ALL: Aah!

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.200
-(JOY GASPS)
-(ALL EXCLAIM)

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.800
(TRUCK ENGINE STARTING)

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.160
Okay, not what I had in mind.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.600
(ALL SCREAM)

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.080
(MUSIC PLAYING)

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.920
JOY: Hey, look!
The Golden Gate Bridge!

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.080
Isn't that great?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.480
It's not made out of
solid gold like we thought,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.280
which is kind of
a disappointment, but still...

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.960
FEAR: I sure am glad you told me
earthquakes are a myth, Joy.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.280
Otherwise I'd be terrified right now!
(CHUCKLES)

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.800
Uh, yeah...

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.080
WOMAN: Are you kidding?
Get out of the street!

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.440
-(CARS HONKING)
-MAN: Oh, for Pete's sake! Move it!

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.560
-These are my kind of people.
-(CARS HONKING)

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.440
DAD: All right, just a few more blocks.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:16.800
We're almost to our new house!

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:17.960
Step on it, Daddy!

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.280
Why don't we just live in this smelly car?

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.800
We've already been in it forever.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.680
Which, actually, was really lucky,

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.360
because that gave us
plenty of time to think about

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.680
what our new house is going to look like!

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.960
What! Let's review
the top five daydreams.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.280
-Ooh! That looks safe!
-SADNESS: That one's nice.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.760
Oh, this will be great for Riley!

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.080
JOY: Oh, no, no, no, no, this one!

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.160
DISGUST: Oh, Joy, for the last time,
she cannot live in a cookie.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.240
ANGER: That's the one!
It comes with a dragon.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.240
JOY: Now we're getting close,
I can feel it.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.880
Here it is, here's our new house.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.400
And...

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.520
Maybe it's nice on the inside.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.440
(DOOR CREAKING)

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.000
ANGER: We're supposed to live here?
SADNESS: Do we have to?

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.080
DISGUST: I'm telling you,
it smells like something died in here.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.200
Can you die from moving?

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.720
Guys, you're overreacting.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.160
Nobody is dying...

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.280
-A dead mouse!
-(FEAR SCREAMS)

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.160
ANGER: Great. This is just great.
DISGUST: I'm gonna be sick.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.680
It's the house of the dead!
We're going to get rabies!

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.240
-Get off of me!
-(FEAR SCREAMING)

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.600
Hey. All through the drive,

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.600
Dad talked about
how cool our new room is.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:18.680
-(FEAR SIGHS)
-Let's go check it out!

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:19.880
DISGUST: Let's go!
ANGER: It's gonna be great!

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:20.960
FEAR: Yes, yes, yes.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.280
No, no, no, no, no.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.600
DISGUST: I'm starting
to envy the dead mouse.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.680
ANGER: Get out the rubber ball,

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.080
we're in solitary confinement.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.160
Riley can't live here.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.240
-She's right.
-It's the worst.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.760
FEAR: Really bad.
DISGUST: It's absolutely the worst.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.240
DISGUST: It's the worst place
I've ever been in my entire life.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.920
Hey, it's nothing
our butterfly curtains couldn't fix.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.320
I read somewhere
that an empty room is an opportunity.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.800
-Where did you read that?
-It doesn't matter.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:39.920
I read it and it's great.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.040
We'll put the bed there.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.200
JOY: And the desk over there.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.520
FEAR: The hockey lamp goes there.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.600
ANGER: Uh, put the chair there.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.120
JOY: The trophy collection goes there.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.800
FEAR: Stars! I like that!

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.000
JOY: Now we're talking!

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.640
Let's go get our stuff
from the moving van!

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.720
DAD: All right. Goodbye.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.800
Well, guess what?

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.560
The moving van
won't be here until Thursday.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.080
-You're kidding.
-Mmm-hmm.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.440
The van is lost? It is the worst day ever!

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.840
DISGUST: That figures. The van is lost.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.640
You said it would be here yesterday!

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.000
I know that's what I said.
That's what they told me!

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.160
FEAR: Mom and Dad are stressed out!

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.080
ANGER: They're stressed out?
FEAR: What are we going to do?

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.720
-(ALL TALKING AT ONCE)
-I've got a great idea!

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.400
Did you even read the contract?

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.000
Andersen makes her move.
She's closing in!

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.080
Hey! (LAUGHS)

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.200
DAD: Oh, no, you're not!

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.320
She's lining up for the shot!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.400
DAD: Coming behind you.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.240
-DAD: Watch out! Watch out!
-She shoots and she scores!

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.920
-Yeah!
-(ALL CHEERING)

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.080
-Come on, Grandma!
-Ha!

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:27.320
"Grandma"?

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.120
Uh-oh, she put her hair up,
we're in for it!

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.760
Whoo!

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.640
-Hey, put me down!
-(DAD LAUGHING)

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:33.840
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.080
(BELL DINGS)

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.680
-(CELL PHONE RINGING)
-Ah! Sorry.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:38.800
Hold on. Hold on.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.720
-Hello?
-Wait. Wh...

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:42.960
DAD: You're kidding.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.440
(SIGHS) All right. Stall for me.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.520
I'll be right there.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.480
The investor's supposed
to show up on Thursday,

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.760
not today!

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.280
-(SIGHS)
-I got to go.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.760
It's okay. We get it.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.080
You're the best. Thanks, hon.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.000
See you, sweetie.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.440
FEAR: Dad just left us.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.120
He doesn't love us anymore.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.360
That's sad.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.000
I should drive, right?

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.640
Joy?

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.440
What are you doing?

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.120
Uh, just give me one second.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.200
Um, you know what I've realized?

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.680
Riley hasn't had lunch! Remember?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.720
Hey, I saw a pizza place down the street.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:18.880
Maybe we could try that?

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.320
Pizza sounds delicious.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.960
-Pizza? That's good.
-Yes! Pizza!

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.800
FEAR: What the heck is that?
JOY: Who puts broccoli on pizza?

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.120
That's it. I'm done.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.280
Congratulations, San Francisco,

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.520
you've ruined pizza!

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:32.800
First the Hawaiians

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.160
and now you!

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.600
What kind of a pizza place
only serves one kind of pizza?

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.000
MOM: Must be
a San Francisco thing, huh?

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.360
Still, it's not as bad as that soup.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.400
-At that diner in Nebraska.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.880
The spoon stood up in the soup by itself!

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.200
RILEY: That was disgusting.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:49.800
JOY: Oh, good. Family is running.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:51.160
RILEY: Dad's got a steel stomach.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.920
The drive out was pretty fun, huh?

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.080
What was your favorite part?

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.800
Spitting out the car window!

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.280
Definitely not when Dad was singing.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.400
Wearing a seat belt!

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.160
Oh! What about the time
with the dinosaur?

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.000
-Oh, that's the one.
-Definitely!

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.800
DAD: Say cheese!

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.360
-Dad! Dad!
-Honey!

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.480
DAD: Now hold still.
MOM: The car!

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.040
Stop! No, no, no! (GRUNTING)

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:10.520
(DAD GROANS)

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.080
(LAUGHS) Nice one, Joy.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.720
I liked that time at the dinosaur.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.400
-That was pretty funny.
-(MOM LAUGHING)

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.080
(GASPS)

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.200
Wait. What? What happened?

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.200
FEAR: She did something
to the memory.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.880
-What did you do?
-I just touched it.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.840
-That shouldn't make it change.
-Change it back, Joy!

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:34.160
-I'm trying.
-You can't change it back?

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.200
-No! I guess I can't!
-Good going, Sadness.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.920
Now when Riley thinks
of that moment with Dad,

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.240
she's gonna feel sad.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.920
-Bravo.
-I'm sorry, Joy.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.240
I don't really know...

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.800
I thought maybe if you...

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.200
(STAMMERING)

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.520
Joy, we've got a stairway coming up.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.160
Just don't touch any other memories

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.560
until we figure out what's going on.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:53.880
-Okay.
-JOY: All right.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.200
Get ready. This is a monster railing

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.240
and we are riding it all the way down!

